Two tables made from one: the old table can be moved into one of them,
not both. Refused, the database unchanged; one table @from the other's
rows and a column @from does a split.

== before
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @drop 1 table menu
-- @from 1 table lunch = menu
-- @from 1 table dinner = menu
CREATE TABLE lunch (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE dinner (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `lunch` is one of two made `@from table` `menu`
table `dinner` is one of two made `@from table` `menu`
